msgid "Where Playground opens once the site is ready: the home page, the dashboard, a page of this site or a path."
msgstr ""

msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

msgid "The language Playground opens in: this site’s, yours or English. Playground fetches the translations of WordPress and of the themes and plugins from the WordPress.org directory; the ones of the others go inside the file."
msgstr ""

msgid "Themes and plugins"
msgstr ""

msgid "What the WordPress Playground .zip installs — any installed theme or plugin, active or inactive as on this site, and must-use plugins (with the folders they load; not the ones the host puts there); a child theme brings its parent, and the active theme is activated if chosen. The ones from the WordPress.org directory are installed from there, in the version this site has; premium and custom ones go inside the file: share it only where their licenses allow."
msgstr ""

msgid "The page is saved as a relative path, /?pagename=<its slug>, so Playground opens the same page whatever ID it gets there."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose a page"
msgstr ""

msgid "The exported attachments’ files (images, PDFs, videos) go inside the file, so the importer doesn’t download them from this site. Off, the importer can still fetch them while this site is online."
msgstr ""

msgid "A plugin .zip holding the bundle: installed on the other site, it imports itself from its screen under Tools."
msgstr ""

msgid "On import, pages, posts and products that already exist on the other site (same slug) are updated with this content instead of getting copies — the homepage stays the homepage, a second delivery updates the first. The importer can still turn it off."
msgstr ""

