#: eizport.php
msgid "https://eizport.github.io/"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: eizport.php
msgid "Export and import WordPress content as .wxrz bundles: the WXR plus its media and content files, gzipped, optionally ready for WordPress Playground. Export several content types at once, each by filters or by selection, with settings."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: eizport.php
msgid "eizport"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: eizport.php
msgid "https://profiles.wordpress.org/eizport/"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:51
msgid "Export and import content as .wxrz bundles or WordPress Playground .zip files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:97
msgid "Get export options"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:98
msgid "Lists what can be exported: content types with their item counts, taxonomy terms, statuses and months; the navigation menus (classic, with their theme locations, and block navigations); the site's look (Customizer theme mods and custom CSS, Site Editor global styles and CSS, widgets); the groups of settings; the default file name; the themes and plugins a Playground .zip can install; the homepage and posts page; how long copies last. Use it before eizport/export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:121
msgid "Get items"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:122
msgid "Lists a page of one content type's items (pages, posts, products, media…) that can be exported: searched, sorted and filtered like eizport/export filters them. Use the IDs in eizport/export \"types\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:144
msgid "The item's roles on the site, from the options pointing to it (eizport_linked_options)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:178
msgid "Get suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:179
msgid "What the items chosen suggest exporting too: \"items\" (post type => IDs, like the products a block in their content shows, or the pages the menus chosen link to), \"reviews\" (comment IDs of the products' approved reviews), \"options\" (settings pointing to them, like page_on_front, as Settings → Export → \"Linked settings\" says) and \"menus\" (the classic menus in theme locations and the navigations their content or the theme's templates use). Nothing is added by itself: pass them to eizport/export to include them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:189
msgid "Post types chosen whole (the same as {} in \"types\"; easier to send in a URL)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:193
msgid "Menus chosen: \"classic\" (menu term IDs); the pages, posts and products their items point to are suggested."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:246
msgid "Get product reviews"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:247
msgid "Lists a page of WooCommerce's approved product reviews (author, product, rating, excerpt), searched, or only the ones in \"include\". Use their IDs in eizport/export reviews.ids. Empty without WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:292
msgid "Get options"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:293
msgid "Lists a page of the site's options that can be exported, one by one (never site URLs, the admin email, keys, active plugins, roles or transients), with their size, whether they are autoloaded and whether they hold a post ID (mapped on import). Use the names in eizport/export options.names."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:303
msgid "Only these options (for instance, the ones chosen)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:308
msgid "Only the options of this group (eizport/get-export-options option_groups)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:334
msgid "The value in a line (arrays as JSON), up to 200 characters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:359
msgid "Export content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:360
msgid "Exports content to a temporary copy on this site and returns its link: a .wxrz bundle (WXR, media and content files, settings) for the WordPress Importer, or, with \"blueprint\", a WordPress Playground .zip that also installs themes and plugins. Without \"types\", everything is exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:379
msgid "Get copies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:380
msgid "Lists the export copies kept on this site (.wxrz bundles and Playground .zip files), with their download link, Playground link and expiry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:406
msgid "Delete copies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:407
msgid "Permanently deletes export copies, by name, or all of them with \"all\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:416
msgid "Names of the copies to delete, as eizport/get-copies returns them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:420
msgid "Delete every copy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:448
msgid "How long copies are kept, in seconds; 0 keeps them until deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:452
msgid "Whether Tools → Export opens the plugin's Export screen. Off, WordPress's Export screen is left as it is, the plugin's is at Tools → Eizport, and classic_ui doesn't apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:456
msgid "Whether Tools → Import opens the WordPress Importer directly (its screen links to all importers)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:460
msgid "Whether Tools → Import → WordPress looks like the plugin's Export screen. Off, the WordPress Importer looks as it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:464
msgid "Whether Tools → Export opens the classic screen instead of the new one (only with replace_export)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:468
msgid "Whether bundles are plain .zip files instead of .wxrz (gzipped tar)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:472
msgid "What a plugin exported \"as plugin\" holds: wxrz (one .wxrz file), root (the bundle's files next to the plugin's) or folder (in a bundle/ folder)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:476
msgid "Whether the CSS rules of an export go between \"head\" and \"tail\" comments named after the file, to show where they came from. The default for exports and imports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:480
msgid "Whether exports of some items bring only their attached media and featured images, like WordPress, without the media they use in their content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:484
msgid "Whether bundles keep each post's content in post_content/<slug>.html files instead of the WXR."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:488
msgid "Who saved export defaults belong to: each user, or the whole site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:492
msgid "When settings that point to exported items (homepage, posts page, shop…) are added: both, check, export or off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:513
msgid "Get settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:514
msgid "The plugin's settings, with their choices: how long export copies are kept, whether Tools → Export is the plugin's screen and whether it is the classic one, whether the WordPress Importer looks like it and whether Tools → Import opens it, who saved export defaults belong to, and when settings linked to exported items are added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:536
msgid "The Export screen's choices: \"types\" (post type => \"ids\" or \"filters\", as eizport/export takes them) and \"settings\" (format \"wxr\" or \"playground\", filename, media, option_names, option_groups, option_all, include_suggested (rows that bring what the items chosen suggest: post types, \"__options\", \"__reviews\", \"__menus\"), review_ids, review_all, menu_ids (\"c:<menu term ID>\", \"n:<navigation ID>\"), menu_all, appearance (theme_mods, custom_css, global_styles, global_css, widgets, advanced-custom-fields), themes, plugins)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:542
msgid "Get export defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:543
msgid "The export choices saved as default (the current user's, or the site's, as Settings → Saved defaults says), which the Export screens start with; empty when none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:566
msgid "Save export defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:567
msgid "Saves export choices as default (sanitized: unknown types, options never exported and themes or plugins not installed are dropped) and returns them. The site's defaults need manage_options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:594
msgid "Clear export defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:595
msgid "Forgets the export choices saved as default: the Export screens start empty again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:619
msgid "Update settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:620
msgid "Changes the plugin's settings given (copy_lifetime in seconds, replace_export, classic_ui, style_import, import_direct, content_files, attached_only, bundle_zip, plugin_content, plugin_import_again, defaults_scope, linked_options, css_markers: one of the choices eizport/get-settings lists) and returns them all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:670
msgid "Import content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:671
msgid "Imports a copy kept on this site, or a WXR/.wxrz file in the media library, with the WordPress Importer: posts, media (from the bundle when it has them) and settings, with IDs mapped. Posts go to the current user."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:679
msgid "Name of a copy, as eizport/get-copies returns it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:684
msgid "ID of a .wxrz, .xml or .xml.gz file in the media library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:688
msgid "Update the posts that already exist (same type and slug) with the imported content instead of adding copies. Default: as the bundle asks (exported with update_existing), else no."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:693
msgid "How the bundle's CSS rules are added: at the end of this site's CSS, at its start, replacing the head/tail blocks of the same name this site already has (replace; with none, at the end), or replacing all of this site's CSS (replace_all). Default: as the bundle asks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:697
msgid "Put the CSS rules between \"head\" and \"tail\" comments named after the file. Default: as the bundle asks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:744
msgid "Post type, as eizport/get-export-options lists them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:750
msgid "Only these items (for instance, the ones chosen)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:808
msgid "Post type => what to export of it: \"ids\", or \"filters\". Omit to export everything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:842
msgid "Ask the import to update the posts that already exist on the other site (same type and slug) instead of adding copies: the bundle's default, which the importer can change. Not with blueprint."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:846
msgid "A plugin .zip holding the bundle: installed on another site, it shows a screen (Tools) that checks the plugins needed and imports the bundle with one click. Not with blueprint."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:850
msgid "WooCommerce product reviews to export with their products: \"ids\" (comment IDs; none: no reviews) or \"all\". Default: all of the exported products' reviews."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:862
msgid "The site's look, in the bundle's options file, row => \"all\" or the keys of the items chosen (eizport/get-export-options lists them): \"theme_mods\" (the Customizer's theme mods: logo, header and background images, colors), \"custom_css\" (the Customizer's Additional CSS, rule by rule), \"global_styles\" (the Site Editor's styles, group by group) and \"global_css\" (its Additional CSS, rule by rule) — block themes — \"widgets\" (classic and block widgets) and \"advanced-custom-fields\" (with Advanced Custom Fields active: its post types, taxonomies and field groups, in ACF's export format). A list of rows means each of them whole. The media they use come along. Default: none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:867
msgid "How the CSS rules are added on import: at the end of the other site's CSS (default), at its start, replacing the head/tail blocks of the same name it already has (replace; with none, at the end), or replacing all its CSS (replace_all). Whoever imports can change it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:871
msgid "Put the CSS rules between \"head\" and \"tail\" comments named after the file. Default: Settings → Export."
